        "Job Location: All Over India",
        "Male: 1.6 KM in 06 Minute , 30 Sec (For Ladakh Region)",
        "Female: 800 Meter in 04 Minute (For Ladakh Region)",
        "Selection Process: Written/Online Exam, PST & PET & Medical Test",
        "Pay Scale:  Rs.21700-Rs.69100/- per month",
        "Visit the official website of Staff Selection Commission at https://ssc.gov.in.",
        "Click on the “Results” tab or section on the homepage.",
        "Look for the link related to “Constable (GD) in CAPFs, SSF, Rifleman (GD) in Assam Rifles Examination, 2025 – Final Result” or similar (check write-up and result PDF links).",
        "Click on the Final Result PDF link (it usually contains the merit list with roll numbers/names of selected candidates, force allocation, etc.).",
        "Download the PDF, open it, and search for your Roll Number using Ctrl+F for quick reference. Save and print for future use.",
        "Online Application:\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tCandidates need to fill out the online application form on the SSC official website during the application window. The form usually includes personal details, educational qualifications, and other relevant information.",
        "Candidates need to fill out the online application form on the SSC official website during the application window. The form usually includes personal details, educational qualifications, and other relevant information.",
        "Written Examination:\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPaper-I:\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tMode: Computer-based test (CBT).\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDuration: 90 minutes.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tQuestions: 100 objective-type questions.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSections: General Intelligence & Reasoning, General Knowledge & General Awareness, Elementary Mathematics, English/Hindi.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tMarks: Each question typically carries one mark.",
